7:> **Build an AI agent that completes a substantial real-world task from start to finish, using neatlogs to trace and improve its runs and Entire to capture coding context and checkpoints, with other partner tools as optional enhancements.**
44:- **NeatLogs**: All three Mastra agents are wrapped with `neatlogs/mastra`, recording agent runs, model steps, tool calls, inputs/outputs, timing, token usage when returned, and errors. CLI and WhatsApp runs have request traces; WhatsApp also records history message count/bytes and reply delivery. Tracing does not trim model context.
49:Set `NEATLOGS_API_KEY` in `.env` to your Neatlogs project ingest key, then restart `npm run bot` (or run `npm start -- "Say hello in one sentence"`). Optional `NEATLOGS_ENDPOINT` selects the ingest endpoint; `NEATLOGS_DEBUG=true` enables SDK diagnostics. Without a key, dashboard export is disabled and startup prints a warning.
51:Open https://app.neatlogs.com and select the project matching your key. Open its traces view and find the `whatsapp.request` or `cli.request` run. The terminal prints the exact `traceId` for each request; use it to identify the run. Expand the agent/model/tool spans to inspect each step. WhatsApp turns share a hashed conversation session ID. Agent/model/tool tracing captures conversation content and tool results; session hashing only hides the phone number in the session identifier.
53:`npx neatlogs doctor --local --json` validates the local SDK pipeline without credentials or network calls. `node --env-file=.env node_modules/neatlogs/dist/cli.mjs doctor --probe --json` sends generated diagnostic spans to your configured project and checks their persisted trace. It does not call an LLM. CLI requests explicitly flush at shutdown; the long-running bot uses SDK batching and signal shutdown handlers.

